### Define React Component Props using TypeScript Interface

Source: https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/learn/typescript.md

Illustrates defining component props using a named TypeScript `interface` for better readability and reusability. The `MyButtonProps` interface clearly specifies `title` (string) and `disabled` (boolean) props, which are then used by the `MyButton` component.

```tsx
interface MyButtonProps {
  /** The text to display inside the button */
  title: string;
  /** Whether the button can be interacted with */
  disabled: boolean;
}

function MyButton({ title, disabled }: MyButtonProps) {
  return (
    <button disabled={disabled}>{title}</button>
  );
}

export default function MyApp() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Welcome to my app</h1>
      <MyButton title="I'm a disabled button" disabled={true}/>
    </div>
  );
}
```

