### Type React Component Props Inline with TypeScript

Source: https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/learn/typescript.md

Demonstrates defining component props using an inline type annotation directly within the component's parameter destructuring. The `MyButton` component expects a `title` prop of type `string` and renders it inside a button element.

```tsx
function MyButton({ title }: { title: string }) {
  return (
    <button>{title}</button>
  );
}

export default function MyApp() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Welcome to my app</h1>
      <MyButton title="I'm a button" />
    </div>
  );
}
```

