### React Timer Component Fix: Correct `useEffect` Dependency Array

Source: https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/learn/separating-events-from-effects.md

This corrected React functional component resolves the stale variable issue in `useEffect`. By adding `increment` to the dependency array `[increment]`, the `useEffect` hook re-runs whenever `increment` changes, effectively restarting the `setInterval` with the updated `increment` value and ensuring the counter increments correctly.

```js
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

export default function Timer() {
