### preinitModule Function

Source: https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/reference/react-dom/preinitModule.md

To preinit an ESM module, call the `preinitModule` function from `react-dom`. This function provides the browser with a hint that it should start downloading and executing the given module, which can save time. Modules that you `preinit` are executed when they finish downloading.

```APIDOC
## Function: preinitModule

### Description
To preinit an ESM module, call the `preinitModule` function from `react-dom`. This function provides the browser with a hint that it should start downloading and executing the given module, which can save time. Modules that you `preinit` are executed when they finish downloading.

### Method
Function Call

### Endpoint
`preinitModule(href, options)`

### Parameters
#### Path Parameters
- **href** (string) - Required - The URL of the module you want to download and execute.

#### Request Body
- **options** (object) - Required - An object containing properties for the module preinit.
    - **as** (string) - Required - It must be `'script'`.
    - **crossOrigin** (string) - Optional - The [CORS policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Attributes/crossorigin) to use. Its possible values are `anonymous` and `use-credentials`.
    - **integrity** (string) - Optional - A cryptographic hash of the module, to [verify its authenticity](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Subresource_Integrity).
    - **nonce** (string) - Optional - A cryptographic [nonce to allow the module](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Global_attributes/nonce) when using a strict Content Security Policy.

### Request Example
```js
import { preinitModule } from 'react-dom';

function AppRoot() {
  preinitModule("https://example.com/module.js", {as: "script"});
  // ...
}
```

### Response
#### Success Response (void)
This function returns nothing (`void`).

#### Response Example
```
// This function returns nothing.
```
