### Migrate React Class Component String Refs to Ref Callbacks

Source: https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/blog/2024/04/25/react-19-upgrade-guide.md

This guide shows how to replace deprecated string refs in React class components with more robust ref callbacks. String refs had multiple downsides and are removed in React 19 to simplify the library. The 'Before' example uses a string literal for the ref, while the 'After' example demonstrates assigning the ref to an instance property using a callback function. A codemod is also available to automate this migration.

```javascript
// Before
class MyComponent extends React.Component {
  componentDidMount() {
    this.refs.input.focus();
  }

  render() {
    return <input ref='input' />;
  }
}
```

```javascript
// After
class MyComponent extends React.Component {
  componentDidMount() {
    this.input.focus();
  }

  render() {
    return <input ref={input => this.input = input} />;
  }
}
```

