### Render React App to Static HTML String

Source: https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/reference/react-dom/static/prerenderToNodeStream.md

This asynchronous function demonstrates how to render a React component tree into a static HTML string using `prerenderToNodeStream` from `react-dom/static`. It collects the streamed data chunks into a single string, suitable for scenarios where a complete, non-interactive HTML output is required.

```js
import { prerenderToNodeStream } from 'react-dom/static';

async function renderToString() {
  const {prelude} = await prerenderToNodeStream(<App />, {
    bootstrapScripts: ['/main.js']
  });

  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    let data = '';
    prelude.on('data', chunk => {
      data += chunk;
    });
    prelude.on('end', () => resolve(data));
    prelude.on('error', reject);
  });
}
```

